# Design-Focused SPA UX

HPCPerfStats serves researchers and operators who expect clear hierarchy, honest loading states, and labels that match data contracts.

## Search results

- Filtered job lists (`/jobs` and equivalent query-driven lists) must show a human-readable **active filter summary** and a **Modify search** affordance that opens extended search.
- API `qname` / page titles must not stay generic **Jobs** when non-trivial filters are applied; use `filter_summary` from the job list API or frontend `buildJobListFilterSummaryLines`.
- Empty result sets return **200** with `nj: 0` and an explicit empty-table message—not a silent error.

## Label integrity

- Job **end time** filters must be labeled as end time (not “start date” for `end_time__gte`).
- Use **`PROJECT_FIELD_LABEL`** from `site-field-labels.js` (currently **Project**) for the charge account field everywhere (extended search, tables, breadcrumbs).
- Table headers use `JOB_LIST_TABLE_HEADERS` where applicable.
- Job list **Performance Data** labels come from the API (`performance.label`). Canonical copy: **Metrics & Plots available** (metrics values + fingerprint-matching plot/detail artifacts), **Metrics available** (values present, artifacts not ready), **Too few samples to complete**, **Too short to complete**, **Metrics & Plots not yet completed** (no `update_metrics` yet; runtime not under the short threshold). Do not claim plots available from metrics rows alone.
- **Job Detail plot tabs** (Summary plot, Roofline, Multiprecision Mix): do not fetch/embed (`job_plots` or multiprecision defer clear) until `job_data.performance.sort_rank === 0`. Plot-tab status copy (not Performance Data labels): ranks **1**/**6** → **Plots not yet completed.**; ranks **2–5** / missing → **No plots available for this job**. Show that chrome **only** inside those plot tabs — never on Metrics or other non-plot tabs.
- **Job Detail Print:** rank **0** → Metrics + Summary + Roofline + Multiprecision (wait for `job_plots` payload + embeds; do not print while `plots === null`); rank **1** → Metrics/overview only (no plot panels); ranks **2–6** / missing → dialog “There is no data to print.” (no `window.print`). Rank **6** is not metrics-only print. During print prep, force-unhide Metrics + plot tab panels (`hidden`/`inert` false) so Bokeh can layout; print-mounted embeds use **`previewMode`** + staggered `embedStaggerIndex`, freeze settled plot/MP payloads, **capture canvas data URLs into React state** (traverse Bokeh 3.x nested **`shadowRoot`s** — see `collectBokehCanvases`) and render static `<img>`s (never mutate React-owned embed nodes), dispose **only captured** targets, then `window.print` after paint. **Hide** unavailable/error plot blocks and all VariableInfoLabel **`?`** help triggers/popovers in print; if capture misses a plot that **has data**, keep the live embed. Never replace existing Metrics tables with Loading-only after print widens defer / refetches (`detailsLoading`); keep tables when `metrics_list` is non-empty.

## Loading vs unavailable vs error

- **Deployment cluster identity** (`host_name_ext`, short `machine` from image ini) is **build-time** via [`site-identity.ts`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/config/site-identity.ts) (`write-site-identity.mjs`); SPA header chrome must not wait on `/api/session/` for cluster name. `/api/home/` `machine_name` is redundant for SPA (retained for `hpcperfstats-tools` CLI). See **`immutable-image-ini-policy.mdc`**.
- **`/machine/**` session gate:** do not mount route `children` until `useSessionRetrieve` resolves; show `LoadingMessage` for session load and redirect shell when unauthenticated ([`app/machine/layout.tsx`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/app/machine/layout.tsx)). Prevents authenticated API queries from firing before session is known.
- **Interactive-ready law:** see **`interactive-ready-controls.mdc`** — hide or skeleton until ready; shown controls must accept clicks immediately; no `pointer-events-none` on table/pagination parents during `tableBusy`.
- Do not show Bokeh **Unavailable** while a section is still loading; pass `isLoading` / `detailsLoading` into `BokehEmbed`.
- Distinguish **no data** (`unavailableReason`), **loading** (`LoadingMessage` / skeleton), and **transient failure** (warning + **Retry** when async fetch fails).
- Unavailable Bokeh plots: generic public **`Unavailable — Data not available.`** status; staff expandable API reason — **`job-detail-analysis-tab-consistency.mdc`**.
- Job list pagination: avoid full-page skeleton when only `page` or `order_by` changes; use `tableBusy` overlay.

## Overlays (extended search)

- Panel uses `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal="true"`, semi-transparent **backdrop**, click-outside and **Escape** close, focus return to toggle.
- Backdrop wrapper uses **`pointer-events-none`** so main content (job table links) stays clickable; panel uses **`pointer-events-auto`**. Outside clicks close via document **`pointerdown`** capture (excluding panel and toggle).
- Call **`onClose`** after successful navigate from extended search.
- Collapse mobile `navOpen` / `extendedSearchOpen` on route change (pathname or query-string navigation).
- Job list **distributions** collapsible defaults **open** on all breakpoints; histogram fetch runs on JobList mount (optional Collapsible collapse after). See **`interactive-ready-controls.mdc`** / **`frontend-stack-wiring-contract.mdc`**.

## Wayfinding

- Machine SPA home is **`/machine/`** (search view). Header/logo and “home” links must use **`href="/machine/"`**, not **`href="/"`** — Django `/` is redirect-only; static export has no `/index.txt` RSC payload at site root (nginx 404 + Next prefetch noise).
- Deep pages include **breadcrumbs** (`PageBreadcrumbs`) or explicit **Back to job** links on type/host drill-downs.
- Shareable primary tabs sync to **`?tab=`** or **`?view=`** (`sync-tab-search-param.js`).
- Unknown SPA routes render **`PageNotFound`**, not a silent redirect home.

## Static export routing

- Under `output: 'export'`, nginx `try_files` serves `/machine/index.html` for deep links; the server-baked `slug` prop on catch-all pages is **not** authoritative after client navigation.
- **`useMachineRouteParams()`** (or `parseMachineSlug` / `parseMachinePathname`) is the canonical source for `/machine/**` view selection and flat route params (`date`, `year`, `pk`, `jid`, `typeName`, `host`, list keys).
- Never rely on `useParams()` flat keys alone when the catch-all shape is `{ slug: string[] }`; tests must set `params.slug` via `configureNextNavigationFromPath`.

## Overlay z-index scale

- In-page sticky chrome (browse tabs, job-detail analysis tabs): **`--z-sticky-inpage`** (10) — beats page content only.
- When stacking sticky in-page chrome with sticky table headers (Job List Jobs/Charts tabs + thead), measure the chrome height (`ResizeObserver` or layout effect) into a CSS custom property (for example **`--job-list-sticky-chrome-h`**) and bind thead `top` plus scroll-margin to that var. Use the same breakpoint as Tailwind **`lg` (1024px)** for JS tab mount and `max-lg:` sticky rules — do not hardcode mismatched rem guesses (`top-14` vs `scroll-pt-28`).
- Modal backdrops (extended search, histogram thumbnail): **`--z-modal-backdrop`** (1040).
- Portaled floating UI (Shadcn popover, dropdown, select): **`--z-floating-overlay`** / `z-[1050]` — must paint above backdrops and sticky in-page layers.
- When adding new portaled overlays, grep for `z-50` and legacy `z-index: 1015` debt; extend `overlay-z-index.test.ts` if the contract changes.

## Forms

- Validation: `aria-invalid` plus Bootstrap **`is-invalid`** and field feedback.
- Primary actions (Find Job, Search) must not fail silently on empty input.

## Feedback components

- Prefer **`LoadingMessage`** and **`BannerErrorMessage`** over ad hoc text/alerts.
- **No toast library** for production SPA; use inline status, banners, and button labels (`Working…`). See `docs/SPA_UI_FEEDBACK.md`.

## Navigation affordances

- Prefer **`Link` / `NavLink`** for route destinations; `<button>` for actions.
- Staff destructive menu items use **`text-danger`**; confirmations stay on the action.

## Tests

- Extend Vitest when changing the above contracts (`JobList.test.jsx`, `ExtendedSearch.test.jsx`, `Layout.test.jsx`, `job-list-filter-summary.test.js`).
- Backend: `test_job_list_filter_summary.py` when changing `build_job_list_qname_and_filter_summary`.

## Overlap

- `react-js-cursor-rule.mdc`, `wcag-aa-mobile-web.mdc`, **`interactive-ready-controls.mdc`**, `search-metric-artifact-sync.mdc`, **`researcher-job-detail-doc-sync.mdc`** when user-visible copy changes — including job-list **filter summary**, **empty results** (200 + in-table message), **Modify search**, job-detail **breadcrumbs**, shareable **`?tab=`** URLs, and partial-load **retry** affordances (update `docs/using-the-website-as-a-researcher.md` §1–§2 in the same task).
